<urn:atm:triage:finding/AJ-FINAL-004-DEAD-IDENTITY-CONFLICT-BRANCHES>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AJ-FINAL-004-DEAD-IDENTITY-CONFLICT-BRANCHES" ;
  triage:title "Dead RuntimeMemberState::IdentityConflict branches remain live in runtime_status_cache.rs after AJ.5 removed the sole producer" ;
  triage:description "Four sites in crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_status_cache.rs still branch on RuntimeMemberState::IdentityConflict (eviction preference in evict_status_cache_entry_if_needed, tally-counting in tally_runtime_member_state, snapshot-all unknown-mapping in build_runtime_snapshot_all, and the conflict_count feeding degraded readiness in finish_runtime_snapshot), even though AJ.5 (commit 926e4d6e) deleted the sole producer, record_identity_conflict, per the team-lead-ruled ADR-045 exception (docs/plans/phase-aj/adr045-exception-aj4-s4-identityconflict.md). The variant can never be constructed at runtime anymore -- these are genuinely dead/unreachable branches, not a functional bug, but a future reader could mistake the conflict_count-driven Degraded-readiness path for live logic. Found by arch-qa during Phase AJ's final holistic gate review; independently confirmed by quality-mgr reading all 4 sites directly. QA source: PR #759 (Phase AJ final gate report). Already dispatched to arch-ctm as part of GO-AJ-FINAL-GATE-1 (team-lead, 2026-08-05) -- not open/unassigned." ;
